27
00:28:53.840 --> 00:28:57.880
So the Community Game Development
Toolkit is a system that works

28
00:28:57.880 --> 00:29:01.720
in the Unity game engine,
which if you're not familiar with it, it's

29
00:29:01.760 --> 00:29:07.040
a big commercial game engine
for making interactive experiences.

30
00:29:07.040 --> 00:29:10.520
And the toolkit— in one of the main things
it does

31
00:29:10.520 --> 00:29:14.280
is simplify how you use it,
because it's a pretty complex,

32
00:29:14.560 --> 00:29:18.760
intimidating piece of software,
but it has a real focus on collage.

33
00:29:18.760 --> 00:29:22.080
So the kinds of source materials
that people use might include

34
00:29:22.080 --> 00:29:25.360
drawings and paintings, 
photographic cutouts.

35
00:29:25.360 --> 00:29:29.800
And then in the lower left
I have a 3D scan.

36
00:29:29.840 --> 00:29:33.680
So you can also
easily make 3D scans with any smartphone

37
00:29:33.680 --> 00:29:37.280
now and incorporate those
into collages in 3D space.

38
00:29:37.280 --> 00:29:40.080
So what do you do with those materials?

39
00:29:40.080 --> 00:29:41.720
You bring them into the game engine.

40
00:29:41.720 --> 00:29:43.280
So here I have an example.

41
00:29:43.280 --> 00:29:47.120
And you arrange them in a 3D space

42
00:29:47.120 --> 00:29:50.320
and you can kind of position and rotate
and scale each object.

43
00:29:50.320 --> 00:29:52.600
Here I have some scans of drawings

44
00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:55.080
and also a

45
00:29:55.080 --> 00:29:58.880
skybox, which is like a 360 degree photo
that forms the background

46
00:29:58.880 --> 00:30:02.000
and you form these
into navigable environments.

47
00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:05.120
So what the toolkit does is
it makes this really complex piece

48
00:30:05.120 --> 00:30:09.760
of software much more approachable
through this lens of collage,

49
00:30:09.760 --> 00:30:13.120
and it abstracts away
quite a bit of the interface.

50
00:30:13.120 --> 00:30:14.960
And also you don't have to do any coding

51
00:30:14.960 --> 00:30:18.480
when you use this
when you use this system.

52
00:30:18.880 --> 00:30:22.800
So I'm going to show you
